ttachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T16:37:49-08:00","id":1051746,"title":"","content":"Uhh, good question, I actually never was clear on that. Let me consult my Talmud and get back to you.<br /> <br /> e: My reading is that when you cast a combined spell, you're generally casting two different effects on the same target(s) unless you spend Reach to separate their scales. Assume that you're casting one single spell that happens to have two effects, but still only uses one set of spell factors as normal. With that in mind, use the lowest of the free Reaches the two spells would grant you, and spend that for your one spell that happens to have two effects. Does that make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 02-19-2017, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T17:07:16-08:00","id":1051756,"title":"","content":"There was a rather lengthy discussion about this on the forums and below was the consensus of how it would be. you can use it if you want or come up with your own.<br /> <br /> Here is how Combination spells are handle in this game. The book is rather obscure when it comes to combination spells and you need to hunt in different sections to peace the entire picture together.<br /> <br /> Your Gnosis will determined the number of spells that can be combined into one casting. It is two at Gnosis 3, three at Gnosis 6, and four at Gnosis 9.<br /> <br /> The may not have a rote in your combined spell.<br /> <br /> You may combine Praxis spells if all spells involved are Praxis spells.<br /> <br /> The following is the Spell Factors for the spell:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> If the combined spells have different spell factors then the mage chooses the primary spell factor. That becomes the Primary Spell Factor for all component spells of the combination.</li> <li><b>Free Reach:</b> Free reach is calculated normally for each spell involved and then you take the lowest number, that is the number of free reaches available.<br /> The use of a reach<ol class=\"lower-alpha\"><li>When using a reach it affects all component spells of the combination.</li> <li>Spell specific reaches can be purchased on a per spell basis and affect only the spell they were purchased for.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Dice Pool:</b> The entire spell has one dice pool and it is figured as follows. Gnosis + Lowest Arcanum + Yantras + willpower (if used) -2 for each spell after the first - Spell Factor modifications.<br /> Dice Pool modifications<ol class=\"lower-alpha\"><li>Yantras affect the dice pool as normal. If using a Yantra it must be relevant to all component spells of the combination.</li> <li>If you take a negative to modify a spell factor it modifies that spell factor for all component spells of the combination.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Each spell in a combined spell is Withstood separately. If a spell has multiple Withstand ratings (for example, a Withstood spell cast with the Sympathetic Range Attainment) it uses the highest rating, +1 for every additional rating.</li> <li><b>Scale:</b> Multiple spell effects must use the same scale unless the mage uses a Reach to separate the effects.</li> <li><b>Potency:</b> Is figured the same as normal and increasing the spell factor with either a reach or by taking a negative to the dice pool. This affects the Potency of all spells involved.</li> <li><b>Duration:</b> Is figured the same as normal and increasing the spell factor with either a reach or by taking a negative to the dice pool. This affects the Duration of all spells involved.</li> <li><b>Range:</b> Is figured the same as normal and increasing the spell factor with either a reach or by taking a negative to the dice pool. This affects the Range of all spells involved.</li> <li><b>Casting Time:</b> Casting time is unchanged and the entire combined spell uses your Gnosis derived casting time for a ritual or if you spend a reach to make it an instant spell then the entire spell is an instant.</li> <li><b>Mana:</b> You must include all mana needed for each component spell used in the combination.</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Since a combined spell cannot have a rote in it this doesn't come into play.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> As an Example: You have Gnosis 6, Fate 4, Life 3 and Death 2. If combining Touch of the Grave (Death \u2022\u2022), Grave Misfortune (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022) and Transform Life (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022) it would look like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> The mage would choose this, smart thing would to choose Potency.<br /> <b>Free Reach:</b> 1 free reach (2 free reach from Fate, 1 free reach from Life and 1 free reach from Death, take the lowest one)<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Gnosis 6 + 2 (Death) - 4 combining 3 spells, +/- Yantras, Willpower and Spell factor modifications.<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Touch of the Grave is not withstood, Grave Misfortune is withstood by Composure and Transform Life is withstood by Stamina.<br /> <b>Scale:</b> The scale for all components is 1 person unless modified.<br /> <b>Potency:</b> The Potency for all components is 1 unless modified.<br /> <b>Duration:</b> The Duration for all components is 1 round unless modified.<br /> <b>Range:</b> The Range for all components is touch unless modified.<br /> <b>Casting Time:</b> The Casting Time for all components is 1 ritual/instant unless modified.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Touch of the Grave (Death \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <br /> <b>Grave Misfortune (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Transform Life (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T22:03:20-08:00","id":1051854,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12852_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode